==English==
{{wikipedia|Paradesi Jew}}

===Etymology===
The first element, which represents a word meaning "[[foreigner]], [[wanderer]]" in many South Asian languages, is ultimately from {{der|en|sa|परदेशिन्|t=foreigner}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One of the descendants of the [[Sephardic]] immigrants to South Asia (where they mostly settled in [[Cochin]] and [[Madras]]) fleeing persecution in Spain.